## Motor Health Decision Logic

The system evaluates three monitored variables:

- Vibration
- Current
- Temperature

Each parameter is classified as:

- NORMAL
- WARNING
- CRITICAL

The overall motor state is determined using the following logic:

| Condition | System State |
|---|---|
| 0 abnormal parameters | NORMAL |
| 1 abnormal parameter | NORMAL |
| 2 abnormal parameters | EMERGENCY |
| 3 abnormal parameters | MOTOR KILL |
| Any CRITICAL parameter | MOTOR KILL |

A critical condition from any individual sensor results in an immediate
motor shutdown.

When a motor-kill condition occurs:

- PWM is set to 0
- L298N IN1 is driven LOW
- L298N IN2 is driven LOW
- Motor operation is stopped
